  "project_root": "/Volumes/Extra/CodeProj/数字人",
  "current_status": "Default readiness no longer opens without real providers; Chinese knowledge retrieval works via FTS5 trigram with legacy scoring fallback; saving settings restarts the sidecar in place; conversation history preserves citations, grounding, and timestamps; Feishu OAuth exchanges through the sidecar and auto-refreshes; conversation and creation support user-controlled recording, transcription, and temp-media cleanup; avatar streams can be started/stopped over the API and rendered as live video in conversation, falling back to portrait if startup or playback fails; knowledge citations are clickable source links, persist across restarts, and can be listed/deleted from Settings; grounded flags are only true when the reply text mentions a retrieved source title; Settings can clear conversation, memory, knowledge, and captured temp media after confirmation; creation requires explicit consent before uploading media to the remote service; Feishu knowledge sync traverses the full Wiki tree and indexes every Docx; empty conversations offer editable suggested questions; long-term memory can be read, edited, and cleared from Settings; all settings and Keychain secrets can be reset in place; advanced model and endpoint fields are collapsed by default; a real-provider acceptance runbook is available; arm64+x86_64 universal sidecar and DMG were rebuilt and smoke-tested. Only Developer ID signing/notarization credentials and real provider/Feishu credentials remain external.",
    "source_refs": [
    "User requirement: package the system as a friendly visual application.",
    "User decision: cloud and local providers share an OpenAI-compatible abstraction.",
    "User decision: use Feishu Wiki as a knowledge source without a separate application account system.",
    "User requirement: integrate all capabilities, provide out-of-box defaults, and keep first-run configuration minimal.",
    "User concern: the proposed onboarding may still feel too technical or burdensome and should be substantially improved.",
    "User decision: technical preparation is necessary before entering the core experience."
  ],
